                <pb facs="0937" n="835" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg835"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/702: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-19T09:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1919,
                                9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 20,
                            6.28 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Three prominent Costa Rican citizens have asked that an inquiry be directed to
                    our Department of State as to whether our Government <pb facs="0938" n="836"
                        xml:id="pg836"/> would consider favorably a request for intervention if
                    presented through me by some of the representative Costa Rican citizens. Owing
                    to great risk of losing their lives it will not be presented unless sure of
                    favorable consideration. They request a reply by cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
